Residual surplus approval (all four categories: router ETH, old-manager BOLD/sBOLD, router BOLD)
├── default zero cap + one atom: precheck aborts (PreMigration.t.sol)
├── actual balance equals immutable approved cap: precheck, import and postcheck pass
│   └── postcheck emits exact unmigrated balances; protocol ETH import remains exact
├── actual balance exceeds cap by one atom: precheck aborts
├── extra donation after precheck: import aborts
├── extra donation after import: postcheck aborts, reverting the atomic Safe batch
└── each cap changes CONFIGURATION_HASH; no setter can widen approval in place

Mainnet-fork fault injection additionally checks real Safe Stage B with router ETH at and above cap.
Above-cap and old-manager exact-ETH donation can still force Safe reapproval by design; these tests do not claim DoS immunity.
